## VS Code Configuration

### Extensions

The following VS Code extensions are recommended for this project:

- [Python](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=ms-python.python)
- [Jupyter](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=ms-toolsai.jupyter)
- [Ruff](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=charliermarsh.ruff)
- [Prettier](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=esbenp.prettier-vscode)
- [Even Better TOML](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=tamasfe.even-better-toml)

### Pre-configured Settings

The project includes pre-configured VS Code settings in `.vscode/settings.json` to streamline development:

1. **Python Analysis:**
   - Auto-import completions are enabled.
   - Diagnostic mode is set to "workspace" for detailed type-checking within the workspace.

2. **Code Formatting:**
   - Ruff is the default formatter for Python files.
   - Code is automatically formatted on save.

3. **Testing:**
   - pytest is enabled as the default test framework.

4. **Notebooks:**
   - Ruff is the formatter for Jupyter notebooks.
   - Automatic formatting is enabled on save for notebooks.

The Python interpreter isn't pinned in settings — VS Code's Python extension auto-detects `.venv` in the workspace root once it exists (run `uv sync` if it hasn't been created yet).

Refer to `.vscode/settings.json` for the full configuration.

